  "slug": "viral-fast-5f30",
  "summary": "Recent work infers path-space divergences and gene-regulatory parameters directly from time-resolved single-cell trajectory data, not summary statistics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is inference of dynamical quantities from trajectory-level data rather than from summary statistics. A preprint estimates functional KL divergence between path-space measures with a scalable data-driven estimator, validated on a benchmark and applied to scRNA-seq trajectory inference. Probability Flow Matching learns biophysically consistent stochastic gene-regulatory dynamics from time-resolved data, and HMCVelo fits deterministic ODE velocity models of methylation and hydroxymethylation per cell and gene. scTrends and scTransient operate on pseudotime, classifying expression trends or detecting transient events. The equation-learning study addresses generalizability of model discovery across parameter space. What is new is treating path-space quantities as direct units of inference. The remaining items, including a Hi-C dissimilarity measure and a glioblastoma ODE digital twin, touch the theme only peripherally.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-04-28"
}
